# Protect top-level planning state files from worktree merge overwrites.
#
# Root cause: worktree branches fork from older commits with stale .planning/
# content. The GSD executor updates STATE/ROADMAP/REQUIREMENTS based on that
# stale baseline. When merged back, Git conflict resolution can replace the
# main branch's current v2.0 content with the worktree's outdated version.
#
# The "ours" merge driver keeps the current branch's version unconditionally.
# Phase-specific files (.planning/phases/**) are NOT protected — those are
# new files created by the executor and merge cleanly.
#
# Setup (once per clone):  git config merge.ours.driver true
.planning/ROADMAP.md merge=ours
.planning/STATE.md merge=ours
.planning/REQUIREMENTS.md merge=ours
.planning/PROJECT.md merge=ours
